* fix(ai-billing): port LLM-billing fence to node-template so forks inherit it (bug.5042 → task.5050)

Operator shipped this in #1779 (merged 2026-06-23). Port the same fence so every
node forked from node-template inherits it instead of reshipping the silent-post-bill
bug (beacon).

- Delete non-streaming LlmService.completion() from the port + litellm/codex/
  openai-compatible adapters + the test fake (surgical, preserving node-template's own
  completionStream + bug.5056 logging). Non-streaming callers drain the stream + await final.
- Broaden no-direct-completion-executestream.stack.test.ts to guard executeStream,
  completionStream, AND reintroduction of completion(); migrate litellm spec + external
  test + container.spec to the streaming path.
- docs/guides/agent-development.md: 'Billing-safe AI: the ONLY way to call an LLM' golden
  path; features/ai/AGENTS.md stops blessing direct LlmService use.

* test(ai-billing): assert logger.error for 500 (node-template bug.5056 operator-fault paging)

node-template's litellm adapter logs operator-fault HTTP errors (402, 5xx) at error,
benign 4xx at warn. The ported [unreadable]/500 test now asserts the error channel
(mocks logger.error too), matching node-template's adapter; 404/401/network stay on warn.

